  ('fb2076d3-f92e-577c-8cca-22ca31edfb93', 'Travis Atkinson', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101823705934421297147', 5.0, 'Wow! First timer from South Carolina. We read this place was popular, so we wanted to try it out. Arrived between 3 and 4, there was about a 40 minute wait. We had a Raspberry Wheat draft (which was delicious) while we waited and sat outside by the fire pit. We shared Santa''s Little Helper for our meal, and it was phenomenal! My made the comment that it may be the best pizza she has ever tasted! For dessert we had the special Apple compote cheesecake. It lasted about 2 seconds. Needless to say, we loved this place. If we were local, we would go all the time.', '2019-09-02 14:42:23'),
