  ('3928d5d7-e7e7-5c26-9d07-e01591137599', 'Juli Hemphill', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113935085090452093619', 5.0, 'Best place to eat & drink in Anchorage', '2018-06-28 03:22:55'),
  ('a128a0e0-1d1b-5d15-a52e-b6adf73bea78', 'Johan Ljunggren', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102627295190177228719', 5.0, 'Best pizza in Alaska...', '2018-06-28 02:35:06'),
  ('da6f5700-9c37-5649-95d6-f8ee8c0796f7', 'Daniel Fried', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107846329760637407601', 5.0, 'Good pizza, great beer, just don''t be in a hurry.  I have been here in Anchorage for 9 years and the Moose''s tooth has never disappointed. The food is always good, plenty of good beer to choose from, but it has become so popular that you can wait for an hour or more for a table.
But it is worth the wait!!', '2018-06-28 02:30:21'),
  ('d168be30-9b3f-5bc8-90a8-588993258836', 'Kelli L', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116101853587613030984', 4.0, 'Love their salads and love all their appetizers. They make their own chips so their nachos are really good. Then their pizza is pretty good, but I think it''s way overhyped. Like it''s definitely a good pizza, but it''s nothing to write home about. You can get decent pizza at Brewhouse for a lot cheaper. Pizza Plaza also has really good pizza, it''s like more traditional Italian pizza.

I still love mooses tooth, but for the fabulous salads and appetizers. The spicy buffalo chicken salad with their house made blue cheese dressing is soooo good. They''ve always got good desserts too.', '2018-06-28 01:51:46'),
  ('891c0dc7-ad19-5738-b38a-b361fc74a591', 'Jesse Halseth', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113784197554462704953', 4.0, 'It''s always busy, because it''s pretty darn good.  The crust is awesome.  The toppings are awesome.  The service is typically awesome.  The beer selection is off the chain.', '2018-06-28 00:02:44'),
