  ('0079f87f-9218-5089-9628-33246d9bfe5a', 'Lakisha Evans', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116985992034605585745', 3.0, 'Went for the Nas concert, which that part was cool but the pizza they were serving was burnt and $6 for a slice of avalanche which was way smaller portioned then usual...kind of sad about that part and they only took cash. Usually never leave disappointed...but it being a concert, I wont hold it against them n will be back.', '2018-06-12 21:02:54'),
  ('ec81d83e-655c-5203-8bc7-925cc64673d1', 'Moe Hanhaz', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106494440049153561156', 3.0, 'Food is great, made sloppy sometimes because they are so busy, service is hit or miss.Better to order for pickup than dining in, long waits.', '2018-06-12 17:59:46'),
  ('ff2bcd2c-c982-56eb-9496-390132af0600', 'Mike Z', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104658144195962542853', 5.0, 'It''s worth the wait!!  I''ve traveled the world and love to find the best pie a city has to offer and to have a place with this kind of quality in our home town is a dream come true.  Not only is there pizza some of the BEST IN THE WORLD, the cream soda and root beer are truly artisan in my opinion.  The Hungarian mushroom soup is a must try.  And although I rarely will order a salad out, I love their salads too! ! !  If you are a beer drinker, which I do on occasion, then you will be impressed with the selection and quality of their brews.  It''s completely understandable why this is the highest grossing, single location pizzeria in America,   The staff hustles and I''ve yet to be disappointed.', '2018-06-12 16:37:13'),
