  ('eefdca81-67eb-5893-9b5c-c128b418d0a2', 'Debi Bloom', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108164165377227818851', 3.0, 'Still waiting for a table for our party of 15. 11 kids ranging from 10 days old to 13 years. It''s been almost 90 minutes. Hope the pizza is good because the kids are crazy! This is our first time eating inside this restaurant and probably the last!
*UPDATE* We did get seated after an hour and a half. The table was already set with plates and cups and water. Our waitress was busy but attentive, and really nice. She was an angel compared to the snobbish girls at the front. The lazy ones who pointed me to the bar when I asked for some water for my 4yo....and since I couldn''t figure out where to go to get her a drink, I took her to the bathroom and used my hand to give her a drink from the faucet. (On that note, at least the bathroom was clean and stocked and looked nice). The pizzas came after about 30 minutes and looked wonderful. I was slightly disappointed that the steak was so sparse on the large chipotle steak pizza. You''d expect a bit more for a $28 pizza. Everything else went well and the pizza was good. There was tons of seating shortly after we were seated....plenty enough for another party or two of 15 to get right in. My advice... plan to go at 9pm or later on a Saturday night if you have lots of kids.', '2018-05-07 06:17:48'),
  ('6f2d4a09-1d67-5fc9-a118-50c62cda9060', 'Ryan Murphy', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112939124565460702030', 5.0, 'Pizza is outstanding', '2018-05-07 06:02:06'),
