  ('47844bd0-78fc-5b64-b120-838be8cfbdd2', 'Brie Tomberlin', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118265006389222766046', 5.0, 'Best pizza EVER!! Totally worth the wait.', '2016-09-08 00:27:29'),
  ('e0894165-4386-5d68-86b1-41048092e1c0', 'Scott Carter', 'https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114940663980948468883', 5.0, 'We didn''t know what to expect when we came here, only that anyone we know who''s ever been to Anchorage has recommended this place. Getting there was easy, but parking sure was interesting. We went during a busy weekend in the Summer, but it''s supposed to settle down when the snow starts coming in.

The place was chaotic and also inviting, we found the "pick-up" line when we meant to walk into the regular entrance for sit-down. There was a long, 40-minute wait, but we knew it had to be worth it. There was a special area for people to have drinks while they waited, and people were coming and going with their growlers like clockwork. All of the staff was super helpful and friendly to us as we admitted we were new and didn''t know how to navigate the restaurant.

When we got seated, our waitress was the absolute best!  She was very knowledgeable with the entire menu, including beers. I opted for the sampler, and let her choose for me most of the night when I wanted something else... she didn''t disappoint! So, the menu... there''s a huge selection of pizzas and things to try, it''s overwhelming how much you want to taste everything. Again, we opted for our waitress''  input and the Amazing Apricot was PHENOMENAL like she promised, we even did a 50/50 so my wife could have her own choice as well. I decided to dig and and embrace the Alaskan way by purchasing my own Broken Tooth growler and getting it filled at the bar. The desserts are great, too. We were taken care of in excellent fashion. Even the bill was reasonable, considering how much we got to experience.

While some may label it was God''s gift to Anchorage, and some may say "meh, my town''s pizza is better".... don''t buy into either. You want a great time, some good pizza, a chaotic-home feel that is still inviting... and you also want to try some house-made beer? This is where you come.

We''ll be back frequently, for as long as we are in the area.', '2016-09-07 19:57:29'),
